30,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"It seems our most successful projects are those with open booking. Conversely, specialist rooms are often idle while general demand is unmet.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"That is concerning. Furthermore, taking rooms out of service has been costing us significantly in off-site rentals. We must prioritize high-utility, low-disruption spaces.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,George,,I've found that our technicians are burdened with manual tasks because the current extraction equipment is inadequate. They are wasting hours on routines.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I've discovered that ground-floor work is a gamble due to hazardous materials, and ""comfort"" projects almost always slip their schedules. We need a project with a clear, mandatory rationale.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,How delightful. It appears our mechanical costs are skyrocketing while we've completely forgotten to fund the replacement of our audiovisual equipment.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@George, if the extraction equipment is failing, that sounds like a mandatory fix. But @Victoria, we must ensure the result is accessible to all.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"Exactly. A project that serves a single wing is less valuable than one that provides general-purpose capacity, especially given the rental costs.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,George,,"The technicians are the ones suffering. If we don't upgrade the ventilation and layouts, the burden remains on a shrinking staff.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, if the ventilation upgrade is an ""inspection"" or ""safety"" necessity, it's more likely to finish on time than a new study commons.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"And if we choose a mechanical upgrade, we must be wary; the market price for ducted plant has risen by twenty percent.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"The data suggests that a general-purpose space, like a study commons or media center, would be highly rated and heavily used.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Victoria,,But we cannot ignore the cost of room displacement. A project that converts an underused hall might minimize those rental losses.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,George,,"I must insist on the ventilation. It is not about ""comfort""; it is about the daily manual labor of the staff.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree with George. A safety-driven upgrade in the labs is less likely to be delayed by the ""comfort"" trap I found in the schedules.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"While I appreciate the logic, we must consider the AV equipment. A media center would be a wonderful way to address the lack of renewal reserves.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"We have a conflict between staff relief and student utility. However, the highest satisfaction comes from bookable, general-use spaces.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"If we can find a balance, the Central Study Commons seems to meet the demand for general rooms without the high risk of hazardous material delays.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,George,,The lab technicians cannot wait another year. Their routines are inefficient and exhausting.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,The risk of hazardous materials is highest on the ground floor. The Study Commons is ground-floor. The labs might be safer.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"A point well taken, Mizuki. It seems the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade is the most rational choice, provided we budget for the market increase.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
