55,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Candidate A addresses the staff issues and is likely a mandatory upgrade, though Candidate B or D would satisfy the demand for bookable space.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Candidate B would solve the general room shortage, but Mizuki's point about ground-floor hazardous materials makes it a risky timeline.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,George,,"Candidate A is the only one that provides immediate relief to our hardworking technicians. It is a necessity, not a luxury.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,I support Candidate A. It aligns with the delivery patterns that actually stay on schedule and avoids the ground-floor risks of Candidate B.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate A is the most logical, despite the rising cost of mechanical plant. It solves a tangible operational failure.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"If the consensus is shifting toward A, I can support it, provided the ""revised layouts"" include some bookable flexibility.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"I am still worried about the displacement of classes, but if it's a necessary upgrade, we must face it. I'll vote for A.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,George,,I am glad we are prioritizing the staff.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,It is the safest bet for the budget and the calendar.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,It is rare that we all agree so quickly. I shall cast my vote for the ventilation.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
